Upstream's fix for "[Windows] Local engine rendering stalls without input
when UI/platform threads are merged" (flutter/flutter issue 192513): pull
request 193181, "[win32] Remove the predicate from TimerThread condition
variable", shipped in Flutter 3.47.6. An engine built from the 3.47.4 tag
on a machine of one's own is the case that issue names; Flutter's own
prebuilt 3.47.x library did not stall. Taken verbatim from the pull
request's diff (base blob 08b69a6d20f6a = this tree's file at 3.47.4).

diff --git a/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/windows/task_runner_window.cc b/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/windows/task_runner_window.cc
